            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "discover_system_state.cpp",
                    "line": 230,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "The common pattern I've been seeing from you is \"if constexpr(ONLY_RUN_APR_ON_POWER_LOSS). How come no constexpr here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "discover_system_state.cpp",
                    "line": 230,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I wanted to avoid extra indentation since \n`!phosphor::state::manager::utils::checkACLoss(hostId)` did not look like\na constexpr to me.\n\nThe result should be the same since the `ONLY_RUN_APR_ON_POWER_LOSS` would be evaluated first and avoid the call to `phosphor::state::manager::utils::checkACLoss(hostId)` in case that's not set.\n\nAgree that it would be clearer to force compile time evaluation of the branch by using `if constexpr`.\n\nRewrote it as 2 statements be more consistent with the other changes.."
                }
            ],
